{:kind :composite, :id :target/penetration-destination, :revision 1, :layer :mid, :doc "Generic wall-through destination selection: marches a ray through block collision up to a resource-limited effective distance and returns the marker position beyond it. The host supplies only a neutral ray/march capability; distance/resource policy remains an input so this composite is reusable by any ability that needs it. Calls plain :target/raycast with :policy {:type :penetration ...} -- see cn.li.combat.host-primitives/query-impl's own docstring for why penetration mode is a data-derived :query-kind override rather than a dedicated primitive, matching the old v2 execution path exactly. Port of the old v2 :target/penetration-destination composite (ac/combat/components/target_penetration_destination.edn) into the v3 model.", :category :targeting, :inputs {:origin {:type :vec3}, :direction {:type :vec3}, :distance {:type :double}, :scan-step {:type :double}, :clearance-steps {:type :long}, :available-resource {:type :double}, :resource-per-distance {:type :double}, :marker-offset-y {:type :double, :default 0.0}}, :outputs {:destination {:type :destination, :from [:local :destination]}}, :body {:component :flow/sequence, :steps [{:component :data/bind, :to :effective-distance, :value {:expr :math/min, :args [{:ref [:input :distance]} {:expr :math/div, :args [{:ref [:input :available-resource]} {:expr :math/max, :args [1.0E-6 {:ref [:input :resource-per-distance]}]}]}]}} {:component :target/raycast, :origin {:ref [:input :origin]}, :direction {:ref [:input :direction]}, :distance {:ref [:local :effective-distance]}, :include-entities? false, :include-blocks? true, :policy {:type :penetration, :scan-step {:ref [:input :scan-step]}, :clearance-steps {:ref [:input :clearance-steps]}, :marker-offset-y {:ref [:input :marker-offset-y]}}, :bind {:hit :destination}}]}}
